    "created_at": "2021-03-12T21:49:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-03-12T21:49:44Z",
    "body": "After further though I'm actually leaning towards *not* requiring a secure context for URLPattern.\r\n\r\nMy rationale is that one of the main uses of URLPattern is as a router within a client-side framework.  It would be difficult for frameworks to have a big chunk of their functionality go away based on the protocol of the site they are used on.  Requiring a secure context would create API adoption headwinds for what seems little benefit.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
